card.statement:
Let $(A,m,\eta)$ be a monoid in $\calC$. Given an $A$-module $(M,\beta)$, then $(V\otimes M, \beta')$ is an $A$-module for any $V\in \ob(\calC)$, where the morphism $\beta':A\otimes V\otimes M \rightarrow V\otimes M$ is defined by

\begin{equation*}
\beta' \ = \
\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]
\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0.25, .25)--(0.25,.5);
\draw[bmod] (0.5, 0) -- (.25, .25);
\draw[bmod] (0.25, 0) -- (0, .25)-- (0, .5);
\btoken{0.25,0.25}{west}{\eta};
\end{tikzpicture}\ .
\end{equation*}

In particular, the pair $\big(V\otimes A, (\id_V\otimes m)\circ (c_{A,V}\otimes \id_A)\big)$ is an $A$-module for any $V\in \ob(\calC)$.
